WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:13.280
What's going on? Do you know what time it is, Roza?

2
00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:15.250
Five fifteen! In the morning!

3
00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:42.110
Roza, you can't turn up the music at five in the morning, dance here like a madwoman and wake up the whole neighbourhood, for God's sake.

4
00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:44.060
That's a disgrace, man.

5
00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:49.160
Well, you could at least once show some understanding for me.

6
00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:50.710
At least today.

7
00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:54.530
And how many of these «todays» do I have to understand?

8
00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:55.900
Just tell me.

9
00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:59.120
Only once a year there is...

10
00:00:59.170 --> 00:01:00.060
A birthday.

11
00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:03.550
Oh, sorry, Roza, that's right.

12
00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:07.540
It's today, sorry, please, what an idiot I am.

13
00:01:08.170 --> 00:01:09.370
Mum, happy birthday.

14
00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:10.280
And what did you buy me?

15
00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:13.340
Burek. What should I buy you at five in the morning, only the bakery is open.

16
00:01:13.390 --> 00:01:14.180
Oh, Mummy.

17
00:01:14.230 --> 00:01:18.810
How fast time flies, it's only been sixty-four years.

18
00:01:18.860 --> 00:01:20.840
Shame on you, you villain.

19
00:01:22.430 --> 00:01:24.160
Come on, march to your room.

20
00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:24.650
March.

21
00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:28.600
And don't come here before ten o'clock.

22
00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:29.390
That's it.

23
00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:30.380
Don't come.

24
00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:50.300
Who is it?

25
00:01:56.390 --> 00:01:57.890
Who is it?

26
00:02:03.980 --> 00:02:06.180
Come on, come on, quickly.

27
00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:27.020
Open up, maybe it's guests.

28
00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:06.850
Oh, look, some flowers for you.

29
00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:08.360
Who sent them?

30
00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:13.840
Well, probably Miša can't come, so he sent you flowers.

31
00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:16.330
Oh no, no, they're not from Miša.

32
00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:17.850
Do you know who they're from?

33
00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:18.610
I don't know.

34
00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:20.130
Do you know who they're from?

35
00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:20.890
I don't know!

36
00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:26.140
Don't shout, I can hear you, the card says: you know who it's from.

37
00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:31.380
It says: to the most beautiful flower from the garden of paradise. Do you know who it's from?

38
00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:33.220
Isn't it Miša's handwriting?

39
00:03:33.270 --> 00:03:36.250
Yes, the florist could have written it.

40
00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:39.100
No, no, no, it's not feminine, it's masculine.

41
00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:41.280
You can recognise handwriting?

42
00:03:41.330 --> 00:03:41.850
Well, yes.

43
00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:42.040
And?

44
00:03:48.130 --> 00:03:48.880
Hello.

45
00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:50.780
Hello, yes?

46
00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:51.580
Hello.

47
00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:54.950
What did you expect? A female voice?

48
00:03:56.560 --> 00:03:59.210
Well, you got a male one.

49
00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:00.960
Yes?

50
00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:01.760
Hello.

51
00:04:03.950 --> 00:04:07.130
Roza, did you perhaps give out my phone number?

52
00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:07.360
No.

53
00:04:07.410 --> 00:04:13.820
But you know what? I often repeat your phone number out loud so I don't forget it.

54
00:04:17.010 --> 00:04:20.250
Roza, you haven't been doing anything silly, have you?

55
00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:21.430
In what sense?

56
00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:23.080
In the sense of silliness.

57
00:04:23.130 --> 00:04:24.350
With men.

58
00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:26.180
Why are you being silly, baby?

59
00:04:26.230 --> 00:04:30.560
I'm surely not going to do silly things with men.

60
00:04:30.930 --> 00:04:33.760
So you did do something silly?

61
00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:36.180
Well, yes, in a way, yes.

62
00:04:37.070 --> 00:04:38.650
How old is he?

63
00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:39.200
Who?

64
00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:42.460
He's my age, I don't like older ones.

65
00:04:42.650 --> 00:04:44.840
So what is this, some friend from secondary school?

66
00:04:44.890 --> 00:04:45.560
God be with you.

67
00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:51.820
Well, where did you meet him?

68
00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:56.250
I think we were together at some protest.

69
00:04:56.480 --> 00:04:59.100
Or maybe at the health centre.

70
00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:00.940
I'm not sure now.

71
00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:02.340
But what's his name?

72
00:05:02.390 --> 00:05:04.540
God, why are you asking me something like that?

73
00:05:04.590 --> 00:05:08.440
Well, you know I've always had trouble with men's names.

74
00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:11.230
Mum, do you remember what Dad was called?

75
00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:13.360
Of course, of course I remember.

76
00:05:14.050 --> 00:05:18.570
We went to music school together for solfège.

77
00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:23.070
Dad never went to music school.

78
00:05:23.430 --> 00:05:28.180
Oh no, not Dad, but this, man, what's his name, yes.

79
00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:31.640
Do, re, mi, fa, sol, la.

80
00:05:31.690 --> 00:05:31.980
La.

81
00:05:32.030 --> 00:05:32.650
Labud (swan).

82
00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:33.320
Lazar.

83
00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:34.320
That's good.

84
00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:38.220
It's good that you remembered before he comes.

85
00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:38.530
Where?

86
00:05:38.580 --> 00:05:39.170
Well, here.

87
00:05:39.220 --> 00:05:39.490
When?

88
00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:42.580
Tonight, man, I invited him to dinner.

89
00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:43.140
To what?

90
00:05:43.970 --> 00:05:48.590
I promised him he'd fall over backwards when he sees how I cook.

91
00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:49.810
You're going to cook?

92
00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:51.570
I invited him to dinner.

93
00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:53.410
Mum, I'm making dinner.

94
00:05:53.460 --> 00:05:55.710
But you're not making apple pie.

95
00:05:55.760 --> 00:05:57.080
I hadn't planned that.

96
00:05:57.130 --> 00:05:59.380
Well, fine. I'll make it.

97
00:06:13.900 --> 00:06:17.350
And for some reason I think you're to blame for this.

98
00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:23.230
Joka, you're negative. You've been negative all day, and Mum has a birthday once a year.

99
00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:27.320
Your mother is a wonder of nature. She has a birthday every year.

100
00:06:27.370 --> 00:06:32.300
Do you believe that I, and even you, have a birthday every year?

101
00:06:32.350 --> 00:06:36.470
Joka, you're being cynical again, and you said you wouldn't be cynical.

102
00:06:36.520 --> 00:06:39.130
Where are my kids? Kids, kids, kids, where are the kids? Come on, kids.

103
00:06:43.320 --> 00:06:46.360
And Rada is our extremely important client.

104
00:06:46.410 --> 00:06:50.040
Yes, she went from a size two to a six.

105
00:06:50.090 --> 00:06:51.710
And Emanuela has breasts too.

106
00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:08.250
Hello, yes, please.

107
00:07:08.300 --> 00:07:12.740
Ah, Olgica, it's you... Yes, yes, I say, Olgica, how are we today?

108
00:07:12.790 --> 00:07:14.110
Sorry? Like a pit bull.

109
00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:19.910
No, for heaven's sake, you'll look like Angelina Jolie.

110
00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:20.820
What are you talking about?

111
00:07:20.870 --> 00:07:21.860
Swelling, a month.

112
00:07:21.910 --> 00:07:23.870
Well, a month is completely natural.

113
00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:29.870
Three months, Olgica, let me tell you, that's completely normal and it's an individual matter.

114
00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:32.170
Yes, don't cry, it will only harm you.

115
00:07:36.620 --> 00:07:44.430
Olgica, I'm not talking to you, please, you just use cold compresses, never warm ones, that's why you swelled up, goodbye.

116
00:07:57.800 --> 00:08:04.260
Jovanka, as a health professional I want to tell you something about jealousy. Jealousy is an excessive fear of loss.

117
00:08:04.310 --> 00:08:06.650
With you it's naturally a bit more pronounced.

118
00:08:06.700 --> 00:08:07.900
That has nothing to do with me.

119
00:08:07.950 --> 00:08:10.590
I have nothing to do with that, I'm not even jealous.

120
00:08:10.640 --> 00:08:13.570
Because I don't give you a reason to be jealous.

121
00:08:13.620 --> 00:08:16.320
Come on, you give me a reason to be jealous.

122
00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:18.170
I would never lose control.

123
00:08:18.220 --> 00:08:18.710
You wouldn't, huh?

124
00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:19.060
I wouldn't.

125
00:08:19.110 --> 00:08:20.500
Well, now we'll see.

126
00:08:20.550 --> 00:08:22.170
What will we see, Jovanka?

127
00:08:22.220 --> 00:08:23.840
Jovanka, what will we see?

128
00:08:23.890 --> 00:08:26.050
Jovanka, you can't leave me here.

129
00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:31.020
Give me the cinnamon.

130
00:08:31.070 --> 00:08:32.290
Well, I don't know where it is.

131
00:08:32.340 --> 00:08:34.470
In the jar, it's right there in front of you.

132
00:08:34.520 --> 00:08:38.260
Oh, here it is, yes, God, I thought it was pepper, you know?

133
00:08:38.310 --> 00:08:42.270
And I was wondering what you need pepper for in an apple pie. Here you go.

134
00:08:42.320 --> 00:08:44.530
Did you squeeze the lemon into the rakija glass for me?

135
00:08:44.580 --> 00:08:47.430
What do you need a lemon for, for heaven's sake, you're not going to drink it yourself?

136
00:08:47.480 --> 00:08:53.240
I told you to squeeze me a lemon and give me that vanillin, to put over the apples so the apples are sweeter.

137
00:08:53.280 --> 00:08:54.850
Why would you need that, God, whatever next?

138
00:08:54.900 --> 00:08:57.910
Are you teaching me, please, how to make an apple pie?

139
00:08:57.960 --> 00:09:00.380
I suppose I know, I've made it a thousand times.

140
00:09:00.430 --> 00:09:04.630
I nicely add vanilla sugar, although I put it in at the end, and I add a little oregano.

141
00:09:05.540 --> 00:09:08.410
Oregano in an apple pie?

142
00:09:08.910 --> 00:09:12.240
Sorry, it's a little, little secret.

143
00:09:13.100 --> 00:09:16.430
Every cook has her own recipe.

144
00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:18.980
I have one too.

145
00:09:19.030 --> 00:09:19.660
Yours?

146
00:09:19.710 --> 00:09:20.060
Yes.

147
00:09:20.110 --> 00:09:20.740
Sizzle.

148
00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:21.140
Ugh.

149
00:09:21.190 --> 00:09:24.440
We're making a really nice pie, aren't we?

150
00:09:25.240 --> 00:09:25.730
Absolutely.

151
00:09:26.280 --> 00:09:28.930
What's the word for a measure of preciousness?

152
00:09:28.980 --> 00:09:30.890
Five letters, the fourth is A.

153
00:09:30.940 --> 00:09:31.380
Money.

154
00:09:31.430 --> 00:09:32.770
No, it doesn't fit.

155
00:09:32.820 --> 00:09:33.590
The first is K.

156
00:09:33.640 --> 00:09:34.490
Then karat?

157
00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:37.440
What else can I do for you?

158
00:09:37.490 --> 00:09:39.830
Maybe you could just turn the oven down to two hundred for me, please?

159
00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:44.760
Come on, you're closer, you turn it down.

160
00:09:44.810 --> 00:09:46.200
Mum, I've been thinking.

161
00:09:46.250 --> 00:09:48.640
Let's put this off for another day?

162
00:09:48.690 --> 00:09:50.020
Don't, son, please.

163
00:09:50.070 --> 00:09:52.210
I need to socialise with someone too.

164
00:09:53.860 --> 00:09:56.730
So what, then you won't socialise with Lazar?

165
00:10:02.790 --> 00:10:04.870
What's this stinking in the oven?

166
00:10:04.920 --> 00:10:09.570
How should I know, man, you were the one making the apple pie.

167
00:10:09.620 --> 00:10:13.060
Oh, Roza, where does a tennis ball in the oven come from?

168
00:10:13.110 --> 00:10:17.070
Oh, that, well, this man who's coming, he likes tennis.

169
00:10:17.120 --> 00:10:22.790
And I thought it would be good for him to see that we have tennis balls too,

170
00:10:22.840 --> 00:10:26.970
but what it's doing in the oven, I really have no idea.

171
00:10:29.260 --> 00:10:34.990
Baby, what would you say if I told you I want to get married?

172
00:10:37.020 --> 00:10:37.710
WHAT!

173
00:11:17.160 --> 00:11:17.810
Hello.

174
00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:19.110
Hello, Beba.

175
00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:31.650
Baby, happy Mum's birthday.

176
00:11:31.790 --> 00:11:32.410
Thanks.

177
00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:34.760
Joka, you look great.

178
00:11:34.810 --> 00:11:37.330
I always look like this.

179
00:11:37.380 --> 00:11:39.350
And you're really handsome too.

180
00:11:39.400 --> 00:11:42.730
You know, you somehow look rested and fresh.

181
00:11:42.870 --> 00:11:46.870
Miša has somehow shrivelled up these days.

182
00:11:47.340 --> 00:11:48.970
From work, you know.

183
00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:53.920
And I have a naturally fantastic complexion and tight skin.

184
00:11:54.840 --> 00:11:56.580
You just keep consoling yourself.

185
00:11:56.630 --> 00:11:58.750
And where are your kids?

186
00:11:58.800 --> 00:12:01.580
The kids are with the babysitter.

187
00:12:04.630 --> 00:12:07.660
I have some important news to tell you.

188
00:12:07.710 --> 00:12:13.100
Okay, let's just hurry, since Joka and I don't have much time.

189
00:12:13.150 --> 00:12:14.560
I'm not in a hurry anywhere.

190
00:12:14.610 --> 00:12:15.770
Well, fine, sit down.

191
00:12:15.820 --> 00:12:19.180
Mum, Joka and Miša are here, but they won't stay long!

192
00:12:19.930 --> 00:12:21.200
Baby, shame on you.

193
00:12:21.250 --> 00:12:21.480
What?

194
00:12:24.030 --> 00:12:24.500
What?

195
00:12:24.550 --> 00:12:27.200
What, what do I have to be ashamed of?

196
00:12:27.430 --> 00:12:29.070
Why are you yelling?

197
00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:29.730
Sit.

198
00:12:29.780 --> 00:12:30.380
Sit.

199
00:12:35.880 --> 00:12:36.140
What?

200
00:12:36.190 --> 00:12:36.770
What «what»?

201
00:12:36.820 --> 00:12:41.620
That I'm standing like an idiot, fifteen minutes I've been standing there at the door.

202
00:12:41.670 --> 00:12:45.600
Joka, please, tell him, he keeps tormenting me.

203
00:12:45.650 --> 00:12:46.460
I will, baby.

204
00:12:46.510 --> 00:12:46.700
You!

205
00:12:46.750 --> 00:12:46.930
Hm?

206
00:12:46.980 --> 00:12:50.530
Do I hear you raise your voice once more tonight?

207
00:12:59.620 --> 00:13:03.390
Mum, my dear mum, we're here, waiting for you!

208
00:13:03.530 --> 00:13:04.010
Quiet.

209
00:13:04.060 --> 00:13:09.180
Doesn't that dress seem a little inappropriate to you?

210
00:13:09.870 --> 00:13:13.090
You could have worn something else.

211
00:13:13.140 --> 00:13:16.710
Why do you think I could have worn something else?

212
00:13:16.760 --> 00:13:18.670
Beba says I look really nice.

213
00:13:18.720 --> 00:13:21.090
Well, fine, if Beba says so.

214
00:13:21.140 --> 00:13:23.090
By the way, I spoke to the babysitter.

215
00:13:31.920 --> 00:13:33.280
I'm for red wine.

216
00:13:33.330 --> 00:13:35.320
Well, why didn't you remind me,

217
00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:37.930
I forgot it in the living room on the piano.

218
00:13:40.220 --> 00:13:41.730
Is the wine coming, Joka?

219
00:13:41.780 --> 00:13:42.830
Thanks, Beba.

220
00:13:45.960 --> 00:13:47.640
Mum has a boyfriend.

221
00:13:47.690 --> 00:13:50.300
Have you heard about the boyfriend?

222
00:13:50.350 --> 00:13:51.570
You have a boyfriend.

223
00:13:51.620 --> 00:13:53.300
Mum has a boyfriend.

224
00:13:53.350 --> 00:13:55.030
Mum has a boyfriend.

225
00:13:55.080 --> 00:13:58.780
Yes, and he's coming here tonight for dinner.

226
00:13:59.240 --> 00:14:03.840
This is going to be a super evening. We're not going anywhere.

227
00:14:07.310 --> 00:14:10.300
So what? If she gets married, I'm free.

228
00:14:10.350 --> 00:14:13.330
Shame on you. Shame on you, you selfish creature.

229
00:14:13.380 --> 00:14:16.860
And some old geezer moves into these rooms.

230
00:14:16.910 --> 00:14:19.610
To enjoy the square metres of our childhood.

231
00:14:19.660 --> 00:14:23.990
The square metres where you and I grew up and spent our youth.

232
00:14:24.040 --> 00:14:29.350
Just so that you wouldn't have to take care of her anymore, to worry about her anymore.

233
00:14:29.400 --> 00:14:31.400
Shame on you, you selfish creature.

234
00:14:58.450 --> 00:14:59.420
Bravo, Beba!

235
00:14:59.470 --> 00:15:01.810
How I love witty guys.

236
00:15:01.860 --> 00:15:02.490
Guys?

237
00:15:02.540 --> 00:15:06.590
Maybe it would be more logical for you to side with the husband.

238
00:15:06.640 --> 00:15:09.060
And you with the wife.

239
00:15:19.500 --> 00:15:23.260
Baby, you and I could go to some play sometime?

240
00:15:23.310 --> 00:15:24.550
Miša hates the theatre.

241
00:15:24.600 --> 00:15:27.140
Yes, Beba is a great connoisseur of the theatre.

242
00:15:27.190 --> 00:15:30.110
He last went to the theatre in 1984.

243
00:15:30.160 --> 00:15:33.080
At the New Year show they handed out little gift packages.

244
00:15:33.130 --> 00:15:34.180
I don't remember that.

245
00:15:34.230 --> 00:15:39.480
If you don't remember, it's because you wet yourself from fear when you saw Santa Claus.

246
00:15:39.530 --> 00:15:44.520
Mum had to take you to the changing room, to the gym, to change you.

247
00:15:44.570 --> 00:15:48.200
And we pulled some ski suit onto you, all wet,

248
00:15:48.250 --> 00:15:52.470
and we brought you home all wet, soaked in pee, at minus seventeen.

249
00:15:52.520 --> 00:15:55.570
We all froze back then, and your pee froze too.

250
00:15:55.620 --> 00:15:58.020
Joka, please, this isn't true, you're lying.

251
00:15:58.070 --> 00:15:59.250
I'll kill you. Seriously.

252
00:16:11.820 --> 00:16:14.470
Roza, happy birthday.

253
00:16:15.040 --> 00:16:17.840
Oh, how nicely you've done yourself up.

254
00:16:18.560 --> 00:16:20.980
I, I did it for you.

255
00:16:21.350 --> 00:16:25.580
Today is your day, nobody is more important than you.

256
00:16:27.650 --> 00:16:30.600
Here, we brought you flowers.

257
00:16:31.460 --> 00:16:33.810
Flowers, oh. Thank you.

258
00:16:35.260 --> 00:16:37.010
That's so...

259
00:16:37.060 --> 00:16:38.670
Generous.

260
00:16:38.720 --> 00:16:41.220
Yes. Generous, yes.

261
00:16:41.900 --> 00:16:43.720
Baby, what did you bring Mum for her birthday?

262
00:16:43.770 --> 00:16:44.780
I made dinner.

263
00:16:44.830 --> 00:16:46.460
Oh, big deal, made dinner.

264
00:16:46.510 --> 00:16:48.580
That was a present, supposedly, left on the piano.

265
00:16:48.630 --> 00:16:50.260
And what, do you want to quarrel with me?

266
00:16:50.310 --> 00:16:52.330
You two, hug right now.

267
00:16:52.380 --> 00:16:52.860
Come on, come on.

268
00:16:52.910 --> 00:16:54.060
No, let's not hug.

269
00:16:54.110 --> 00:16:56.270
No, no, no hugging, I'm a bit under the weather.

270
00:16:56.420 --> 00:17:02.220
Jovanka, sit down, let's have dinner, and then you can meet my beloved.

271
00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:07.000
Lazar.

272
00:17:07.050 --> 00:17:09.700
Which beloved Lazar?

273
00:17:11.740 --> 00:17:14.320
Mum, I'm shocked.

274
00:17:14.400 --> 00:17:15.870
A younger boyfriend?

275
00:17:15.920 --> 00:17:18.870
No, a couple of years older.

276
00:17:19.220 --> 00:17:22.620
So, does that old man want something from you?

277
00:17:24.180 --> 00:17:27.250
Picasso became a father at eighty.

278
00:17:27.300 --> 00:17:29.320
Jovanka, that's disgusting.

279
00:17:29.370 --> 00:17:32.870
Some men stay interested for longer.

280
00:17:37.400 --> 00:17:38.740
Jovanka, come on, enough.

281
00:17:38.790 --> 00:17:39.570
Why, Miša?

282
00:17:40.320 --> 00:17:42.770
And when Mum gets married, what will you do?

283
00:17:42.820 --> 00:17:45.720
Who will you belong to? Where will you live?

284
00:17:45.770 --> 00:17:47.130
I thought with you.

285
00:17:47.180 --> 00:17:50.210
Sure, of course. Miša is never home anyway.

286
00:17:50.260 --> 00:17:53.480
No, it's not possible. We don't have enough room in the bed.

287
00:17:53.530 --> 00:17:57.010
Well, I have a sleeping bag, I can sleep on the terrace.

288
00:17:57.060 --> 00:17:59.450
No, you can't, you'll freeze on the terrace.

289
00:18:04.480 --> 00:18:07.260
I can look after your kids, so we'd sleep like brothers.

290
00:18:07.310 --> 00:18:10.610
No, that doesn't help. That wouldn't stop the rumours at all.

291
00:18:11.760 --> 00:18:12.690
What rumours?

292
00:18:12.740 --> 00:18:22.820
Oh nothing, I mean, friends often ask me like: what's up with your brother, is everything okay, like, you know, is he maybe gay or something.

293
00:18:22.870 --> 00:18:23.800
God forbid.

294
00:18:23.850 --> 00:18:25.130
And what do you tell them?

295
00:18:25.180 --> 00:18:28.000
I tell them you're a macho man.

296
00:18:28.050 --> 00:18:28.620
Thank you.

297
00:18:28.670 --> 00:18:34.710
A macho man, except that you do the washing, ironing, cooking, live with Mum and don't go out with women.

298
00:18:34.760 --> 00:18:37.080
Yes. What do you expect others to think?

299
00:18:37.130 --> 00:18:45.330
Well, maybe they'd think there is a man who puts his family above everything and doesn't chase every woman who walks by.

300
00:18:45.380 --> 00:18:49.680
Kids, I read somewhere that being gay is okay.

301
00:18:53.200 --> 00:18:56.980
People, I'm going to see what's up with the pie.

302
00:19:14.260 --> 00:19:18.420
Don't listen to Miša. He has no idea what a real man is.

303
00:19:18.470 --> 00:19:21.180
True, but I'm far from a macho man.

304
00:19:21.230 --> 00:19:23.550
You're a man with many good qualities.

305
00:19:23.600 --> 00:19:27.170
That's right, I knit, wash, cook, help elderly people.

306
00:19:27.220 --> 00:19:30.060
You're caring, gentle, kind, full of understanding.

307
00:19:30.110 --> 00:19:32.170
But women don't like such men.

308
00:19:32.220 --> 00:19:33.090
That's not true.

309
00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:40.870
I have to check the oven.

310
00:19:40.920 --> 00:19:41.800
Give it here, I'll do it.

311
00:19:41.850 --> 00:19:43.650
Don't, careful, it's hot.

312
00:20:00.970 --> 00:20:03.360
I burned my little finger. Baby, blow on it.

313
00:20:03.410 --> 00:20:06.480
Why should he blow on it? I'll blow on it!

314
00:20:06.530 --> 00:20:08.230
And you're telling me things!

315
00:20:08.280 --> 00:20:14.020
And I'll tell you, a hippie movement and a hippie commune is one thing, and a daughter-in-law is another, you know?

316
00:20:14.070 --> 00:20:16.570
By the time I count to five!

317
00:20:16.630 --> 00:20:20.330
Everybody be in the dining room, I'm opening up!

318
00:20:21.240 --> 00:20:21.960
One!

319
00:20:38.500 --> 00:20:41.040
Tell me what happened in the kitchen.

320
00:20:41.090 --> 00:20:44.680
Nothing, darling, I burned my little finger, look.

321
00:20:44.730 --> 00:20:46.460
Do you want to blow on it, please?

322
00:20:46.510 --> 00:20:48.160
Blow, it'll be easier for me.

323
00:20:48.210 --> 00:20:52.690
I'm not going to blow on your little finger, I want to know what happened.

324
00:20:52.740 --> 00:20:54.390
Nothing happened.

325
00:20:54.440 --> 00:20:55.520
Here, this is...

326
00:20:55.570 --> 00:20:56.000
Lazar.

327
00:20:56.050 --> 00:20:59.240
Lazar, you remembered well, that's right, Lazar.

328
00:20:59.290 --> 00:21:05.550
Thanks, my real name is Slavko, but since Rosa calls me Lazar, let it stay that way.

329
00:21:06.520 --> 00:21:10.970
Wow, Rosa, you look phenomenal tonight.

330
00:21:12.230 --> 00:21:13.550
Wow, Lazar.

331
00:21:16.700 --> 00:21:23.400
Now meet my family: this is my son Miša, brilliant, very successful.

332
00:21:24.590 --> 00:21:31.140
Professor Popović, Doctor Miša, plastic surgeon, you've surely heard of me.

333
00:21:32.280 --> 00:21:38.000
Slavko Lazar, academic, a professor too, but also a professor of life.

334
00:21:38.830 --> 00:21:43.800
School for apprentices in industry, semi-secondary vocational qualification.

335
00:21:44.330 --> 00:21:47.190
And this is my daughter-in-law Jovanka.

336
00:21:57.680 --> 00:22:00.610
They have two wonderful children, yes.

337
00:22:00.660 --> 00:22:04.560
And did you meet Mum at solfège?

338
00:22:04.610 --> 00:22:09.730
No, we've only known each other recently. We met through...

339
00:22:35.720 --> 00:22:38.840
If you didn't exist, you'd have to be invented.

340
00:22:38.890 --> 00:22:41.520
I hear your mother adores you.

341
00:22:41.570 --> 00:22:45.610
I'm jealous of you, I envy you, you know.

342
00:22:59.020 --> 00:23:09.100
Rosica, since we're alone, I think the two of us could now raise a toast to your birthday and to your wonderful family.

343
00:23:09.700 --> 00:23:12.580
Jovanka, don't be silly!

344
00:23:34.940 --> 00:23:39.590
Lovebirds, youth, madness, they just chase each other all day long.

345
00:23:39.640 --> 00:23:41.070
Yes, they're lovely.

346
00:23:50.500 --> 00:23:57.800
I apologise, I would suggest we all go somewhere, the four of us, to a restaurant.

347
00:23:59.120 --> 00:24:02.350
The oven broke, the heating element burst.

348
00:24:02.400 --> 00:24:05.430
In short, we're left without dinner.

349
00:24:20.780 --> 00:24:23.880
A toast, gentlemen, a toast.

350
00:24:26.360 --> 00:24:34.710
Our dear Roza Rosica, like a dewy flower, there's nobody who wouldn't want you, all for you and your happiness.

351
00:24:45.880 --> 00:24:50.330
Three times wow for our Rosa, please. Wow, wow, wow.

352
00:24:55.040 --> 00:25:01.370
Oh, Lazar, come with me to the kitchen, help me with the dinner, come on.

353
00:26:16.250 --> 00:26:22.650
Baby, it seems you were right. There really is something wrong with the oven.

354
00:26:59.240 --> 00:27:02.790
I can't answer the phone anymore.

355
00:27:02.840 --> 00:27:06.490
People call me and hang up on me.

356
00:27:12.610 --> 00:27:15.260
I placed an ad, yes.

357
00:27:15.430 --> 00:27:17.930
And what's your name?

358
00:27:17.990 --> 00:27:18.960
Milenko.

359
00:27:19.010 --> 00:27:19.480
Aha.

360
00:27:19.530 --> 00:27:22.180
A retired lawyer, yes.

361
00:27:22.340 --> 00:27:24.340
I'm Rozalija.

362
00:27:24.390 --> 00:27:26.520
They call me Roza, yes.

363
00:27:26.570 --> 00:27:29.440
I'm an eternal rebel.

364
00:27:31.370 --> 00:27:35.970
And tell me, do you like apple pie?
